    "result_text": "The build is green. The only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (plus the base/capture support classes), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` becomes `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after this create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing snapshot-at-create pattern (like `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`), the household size is computed and persisted at creation time so it can be derived on read-back:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter, and updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `GOLD` first when `householdSize >= 3`, falling through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic otherwise.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 after household assignment in `addOwner`, it sets `householdSize` via a new `householdSizeAfterCreate(householdId)` helper. The helper counts existing owners sharing the `householdId` and adds 1 for the not-yet-persisted new owner (a null household = size 1).\n- **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column. Tests use the hsqldb profile; the others were updated for consistency.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule (it's a free-form string, no enum, so no value constraint needed).\n\nIn the test, the first two shared-household members are created with household sizes 1 and 2 (not GOLD), and the third snapshots size 3 \u2192 GOLD, which the read-back asserts.",
